WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.600
This is the D-Drive perception stack running against three road profiles in sequence.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.600
What you are looking at is not a recording of a drive.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.100
The vehicle model is solved in real time.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:19.100
550 kilograms, a 2.1 meter wheelbase, and a tire friction coefficient of 0.75.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:24.600
Steering angle and lateral acceleration follow from that physics, not from an animation path.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.100
The center panel is the planner's bird's eye view,

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.600
and it redraws from the fused object list rather than from the scene.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:37.100
On the right, the perception rail names each object it has classified and gives its range in meters.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.600
A motorbike, an auto rickshaw, a pedestrian.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:46.100
Watch the scenario change from Market Street to Single Carriageway Highway to the deliberate stress test.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.600
The same stack handles all three.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.600
Nothing is reloaded between them and no parameters are retuned.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.600
That is the point of the demonstration.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:00.600
One perception pipeline on one chip across the road conditions an Indian commercial vehicle actually meets.
